# File: specs/319-remediate-failing-hosted-checks-that-are-not-branch-protected/feature.gherkin
#
# Generated from: specs/319-remediate-failing-hosted-checks-that-are-not-branch-protected/requirements.md
Feature: Remediate failing hosted checks that are not branch-protected
  Delivery previously polled forever when required checks passed and a
  non-required hosted check failed. The snapshot now includes every
  gh pr checks result so failing non-required checks emit remediation.

  # --- Bug Is Fixed ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Failing non-required hosted check emits remediation
    Given an open delivery PR whose required checks passed
    And a non-required hosted check named "Validate nmg-sdlc contribution evidence" failed
    And GitHub reports mergeStateStatus UNSTABLE
    When the delivery controller observes that PR
    Then it exits 3 with NMG_SDLC_REMEDIATION
    And failingChecks includes "Validate nmg-sdlc contribution evidence"
    And it does not sleep in the mergeability_pending poll loop

  # --- Related Behavior Still Works ---

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Pending and merge-ready classification is preserved
    Given a delivery PR whose hosted checks are all pending or all successful
    When the delivery controller observes that PR
    Then pending checks still classify as pending
    And successful exact-head CLEAN PRs still classify as merge_ready
    And human-review threads, CHANGES_REQUESTED, and required-check failures keep their current statuses
